Pixal3D Vulkan port for MediaForge

Projection mathematics in native/projection.cpp are adapted from
TencentARC/Pixal3D, revision f7cf38429b0bd264f1995f0f8743a88b1c728b94,
pixal3d/trainers/flow_matching/mixins/image_conditioned_proj.py.
Copyright (c) 2026 Tencent. MIT license: see LICENSE.pixal3d.

Changes: C++ front-view coordinate planning, GGML feature sampling, explicit
backend selection, sparse index order preservation and numerical test driver.
This component does not include model weights.

trellis.cpp and its GGML checkout are external, pinned build dependencies;
their notices and licenses remain in those source/runtime distributions.

The projected DiT patch modifies trellis.cpp include/dit.h and src/dit.cpp,
revision 2516c48b677050c570f47eba2e68dc8a5bc918b0.
Copyright (c) 2026 Piotr Wilkin. MIT license: see LICENSE.trellis.
Changes: optional per-block projected conditioning, strict input checks and
opt-in F32 GELU for numerical parity. The original runtime is not modified.

native/flow_runner.cpp adapts GGUF loading, timestep embedding and RoPE formulas
from trellis.cpp src/trellis_model.cpp and src/flow_runner.cpp at the same pin.
Its Euler/CFG/interval sampling follows TencentARC/Pixal3D
pixal3d/pipelines/samplers/{flow_euler,classifier_free_guidance_mixin,
guidance_interval_mixin}.py and modules/sparse/basic.py at the pin above.
Changes: borrowed explicit backend, typed positive/negative projected conditions,
fixed texture concatenation, bounded validation, cancellation/progress hooks,
graph reuse and non-finite failure instead of silent numerical repair.
These adaptations are covered by the corresponding MIT licenses above.

native/image_features.cpp adapts the DINOv3 GGML graph from trellis.cpp
src/dinov3.cpp at the pinned revision above. Changes: configurable dimensions,
strict input/weight validation, ImageNet normalization, explicit backend support
checks, resource cleanup, CLS/register/patch splitting and diagnostic outputs.
Image feature selection, LR/HR projection concatenation and zero negative
conditioning follow TencentARC/Pixal3D's image_conditioned_proj.py at its pin.
prepare_image.py preserves the reference Pillow resize/RGB order. Foreground
removal, NAF, MoGe and pretrained model weights are not included in this slice.

native/naf.cpp ports the evaluation encoder, adaptive pooling, key/value resize
and neighborhood attention architecture from valeoai/NAF, revision
37f2dfc180f2de53d98bd601109c0da0dd6b0f43,
src/model/naf.py and src/layers/{attentions,convolutions}.py.
Copyright the NAF authors. Apache-2.0 license: see LICENSE.naf.
Changes: C++/GGML graphs, explicit caller backend, reflected convolution padding,
separable adaptive pooling, bounded tiles, persistent Q/K/V, cancellation,
validation and synthetic numerical comparison. No trained weights are included.
The positional half-rotation graph reuses our trellis-derived image_features.cpp
construction above; NAF's Python rope.py (which carries a separate DINOv3 notice)
is executed as an external reference, not copied into this distribution.

Neighborhood border/residue mathematics follow NATTEN 0.21.0's
natten/backends/flex.py, copyright (c) 2022-2025 Ali Hassani, MIT license:
see LICENSE.natten. Changes: native index planning with nearest-exact LR mapping,
without copying or introducing a GPU kernel. The CPU checker calls the installed
original NATTEN flex backend, splitting/padding V channels as required by that
backend, instead of NAF's hard-coded cutlass backend. This is not a cutlass or
Vulkan acceptance result.

native/vision_checkpoint.cpp adapts local GGUF container/weight loading from
the pinned trellis.cpp src/trellis_model.cpp (MIT, LICENSE.trellis), using a
borrowed backend and an owned file handle. Changes: strict vision metadata and
tensor/file-extent validation, finite-value checks, exception cleanup, and
DINO/NAF image-feature orchestration without device selection or fallback.
convert_vision.py maps the public Hugging Face DINOv3ViTModel parameter layout
from transformers4.57.3 and the pinned NAF state_dict into the existing native
graphs. It does not copy model implementation code or include trained weights.

prepare_image.py foreground framing and native/stage_bridge.cpp follow pinned
TencentARC/Pixal3D pixal3d/pipelines/pixal3d_image_to_3d.py (MIT above).
Changes: explicit removal-provider boundary, strict dimensions, native stage
handoffs and actual run() cascade planning, with synthetic numerical checks.

native/ss_decoder.cpp adapts pinned trellis.cpp src/ss_decoder.cpp (MIT above)
to configurable spatial/channel extents, exact Pixal normalization placement,
F32 evaluation, strict backend support, cancellation/progress and RAII cleanup.
Its checkpoint loader follows our strict vision loader derived from trellis.cpp.
The architecture and parameter layout follow pinned TencentARC/Pixal3D
pixal3d/models/sparse_structure_vae.py (MIT above), which is run externally as
the numerical reference. No pretrained weights are included.

native/sparse_decoder.cpp and convert_sparse_decoder.py follow the pinned
TencentARC/Pixal3D sc_vaes/sparse_unet_vae.py and fdg_vae.py parameter layout,
ConvNeXt/C2S architecture and modules/sparse/spatial/spatial2channel.py ordering
(MIT, LICENSE.pixal3d). The GGML graph/loader structure also adapts the pinned
trellis.cpp sparse.cpp/shape_decoder.cpp and our strict loaders (MIT above).
Changes: explicit borrowed backend, configurable stages/width, one gathered
im2col GEMM per chunk, selected-child-only C2S output, strict coordinate/guide
alignment and bounds, cancellation/progress, RAII and raw-field diagnostics.
No GPU kernels or trained weights are included.

sparse_cpu_reference.py loads external, pinned FlexGEMM revision
6dd94a859c26ee8246888502eada3dd8ad85532e,
flex_gemm/ops/spconv/submanifold_conv3d.py's Torch neighbor and explicit-GEMM
reference methods via AST extraction. It executes original source locally,
without copying that implementation or importing its GPU autotuning kernels.
The Pixal sparse-conv dispatcher is adapted only inside the evaluation process;
the external files and production model implementation remain unchanged.

native/mesh_decode.cpp follows pinned trellis.cpp src/dual_grid.cpp (MIT above)
and Microsoft TRELLIS.2 revision 75fbf0183001ed9876c8dbb35de6b68552ee08bd,
o-voxel/o_voxel/convert/flexible_dual_grid.py. Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation,
MIT license: see LICENSE.trellis2. Pixal's FDG head and PBR affine conversion
follow fdg_vae.py and pixal3d_image_to_3d.py at the pinned Pixal revision above.
Changes: validated coordinates/fields/margin, configurable actual grid, bounded
triangle count, cancellation/progress, shared shape-to-texture subdivisions and
an explicit unrepaired surface intermediate. No GPU kernel is introduced.

check_mesh_decode.py executes the original o_voxel triangulation and Pixal FDG
class/texture method locally. Only GPU hashmap insertion/lookup is replaced by
a CPU dictionary preserving in-grid lookup and uint32 missing-index semantics.
It loads original source via AST without importing GPU-only cumesh dependencies.
This is not acceptance of o_voxel GPU kernels or CuMesh hole filling.
